    description: "Fresh BROAD cohort (chatwoot) found 19 Symbol.language='erb' violations. _view_template_core.py:251 stamps language from view_template.py's _EXTENSION_LANGUAGE map ('.html.erb'->erb, also 'haml','slim'). erb/haml/slim are real Rails view-template languages (like markdown/asciidoc) but are neither registered analyzer languages nor taxonomy.LANGUAGES LanguageSpecs, so the WI-kunut taxonomy-union does not cover them. FIX: add LanguageSpec(name='erb'|'haml'|'slim', extensions=[...], roles=...) to taxonomy.py. NEEDS HUMAN CALL: the roles= choice (CONFIG like html vs DOCUMENTATION) has file-discovery/LOC side-effects; and confirm batching haml/slim. FOLD-to-ruby rejected (an .html.erb is an HTML template with embedded Ruby, not Ruby source)."  # 632e
